-- title:
--   Leading residue and dominance at the index m
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e, q \ge 1$ be natural numbers. Work in the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)`, the quotient of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi^e$. Let $x \neq 0$ be an element of this model, and let $ab = (a,b)$ be a pair of one-variable power series over $W$ with $b$ having zero constant term, such that the class of $\mathrm{inU}\,a + \mathrm{inV}\,b$ is $x$; here $\mathrm{inU}\,a$ is the bivariate series with coefficient $a_i$ at $(i,0)$ and zero elsewhere, and $\mathrm{inV}\,b$ the one with coefficient $b_j$ at $(0,j)$ and zero elsewhere, so that $(a,b)$ is a normal form for $x$. Let $\gamma$ be a unit of the model, represented by a bivariate power series $G$, and let $m$ be a natural number with $x - \gamma \cdot U(\varpi^e)^m$ in the ideal generated by the class of $\varpi$ and by $V(\varpi^e)$, where $U(\varpi^e)$ and $V(\varpi^e)$ are the two coordinates of the model. Then two things hold. First, the leading residue $\mathrm{leadingResidue}\,\varpi$ of the normal-form coefficient $\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,ab\,(m) = a_m$ — that is, $0$ if $a_m = 0$ and otherwise the residue class of the chosen unit quotient of $a_m$ by the maximal power of $\varpi$ dividing it — equals the residue class of the constant coefficient of $G$ in the residue field of $W$. Second, $m$ (as an integer) lies in $\mathrm{dominantIndices}$ for the order function $w \mapsto q \cdot \mathrm{addVal}_W(w)$, weight exponent $q e$ and depth parameter $0$: the term order $q\,\mathrm{addVal}_W(a_m)$ plus the annulus weight of the multi-index attached to $m$ equals the infimum, over all multi-indices $d$, of $q\,\mathrm{addVal}_W$ of the $d$-th coefficient of $\mathrm{inU}\,a + \mathrm{inV}\,b$ plus the annulus weight of $d$.
--
--   This is the statement at the $U$-branch of the crossing model: congruence of $x$ with $\gamma U^m$ modulo $(\varpi, V)$ pins down both the leading residue of the $m$-th normal-form coefficient and the dominance of the index $m$ for the Gauss-type order attached to the annulus with parameters $qe$ and $0$. It is formulated on the coefficient itself rather than on the initial form at the closed end, and feeds the end step of the node telescoping used for the specialisation of divisors, as well as the computation of leading residues of characteristic-polynomial coefficients.
